tree c16e4a0bc97d4879fb43dcfc58c5c2e9e510cefc
parent 8ea9ad7007c291b9f892d555422255dbec95280a
author alexeikarp <ak@hrbr.life> 1790277173 +0400
committer alexeikarp <ak@hrbr.life> 1790277173 +0400

fix(shared): GrainCert requires the app's GlobalAppApproval Active, with no revoked_at, before the author clearance (R-15c)

8ea9ad70 made GrainCert read the app's GlobalAppApproval for its author and
deliberately left the status unjudged. The authz launch path does judge it:
its cascade requires the global tier Active (pkg/grainauth cascade.go
CascadeVerify and EvalCachedCascade: Revoked is cascade-blocked:global:revoked,
RevokingCascadeInProgress is cascade-blocked:global:revoking-cascade-in-progress,
any other value is unknown and denies), and gate.go decides the cascade before
its App and Author blacklist stage. GrainCert still verified an artifact of an
app the Foundation had revoked, or was revoking.

verify (identity-gate)
- RequireActiveGlobalAppApproval(a) passes only status Active with revoked_at
  None. Revoked is ErrGlobalAppApprovalRevoked, RevokingCascadeInProgress is
  ErrGlobalAppApprovalRevokingCascadeInProgress, Active with a revoked_at is
  ErrGlobalAppApprovalRevokedAtWhileActive, and an out-of-range status is
  refused as unknown. Every refusal also matches ErrStatusNotActive.
- RequireCanonicalGlobalAppApproval is unchanged and still does not judge
  status. Its doc now points to the new function.

How this lines up with authz: authz origin/main (3e14223) decides on the status
byte alone. It decodes revoked_at as a well-formed Option but does not judge it.
The revoked_at None requirement follows R-14's reading of the licence. It only
refuses a state the program never writes: approve_global_app sets Active with
revoked_at None (instructions/app_approval.rs:80-82), and each revoked_at = Some
write sets Revoked (:134-135, :186-187). So GrainCert and authz decide the same
way on every approval the program can hold. revoke_reason is not judged, same
as in authz.

GrainCert
- R-15c: after R-15b binds the approval to the app and Foundation, and before
  R-15 reads any clearance, VerifyGrainCert calls RequireActiveGlobalAppApproval.
  A refusal is the new ErrAppApprovalNotActive and wraps the verify cause, which
  names the state. The author the approval names is still R-15's Author target,
  and the clearance order (app, author, licence) is unchanged.
- PROVENANCE_CONTRACTS.md: the chain-read table, the R-15b row (status is now
  R-15c's), a new R-15c row, and 9.6(f). doc.go row ownership lists R-15c.

Vectors: pda/testdata/contracts-global-app-approval now holds one
GlobalAppApproval per ApprovalStatus, all encoded by the contracts
(licence-registry-model.mjs encodeAccount), decoded back by the contracts'
decoder and located at the address the contracts derive. The new account,
"revoking", is RevokingCascadeInProgress with revoked_at and revoke_reason
None, which is what revoke_global_app_chunk leaves before its final chunk.
gen_global_app_approval_vectors.mjs regenerated the file from a clean export of
contracts origin/main 23007dc6. The active and revoked accounts and the header
are unchanged, byte for byte. New SHA-256: cad37fea...abf4e. The provenance
test now also pins instructions/app_approval.rs (blob aa12fc77), because the
three accounts' field values follow that file's writes. The other three source
blobs are the same as at 9aefcf7d. The vector test requires one account per
status and checks each verdict: active passes, revoked is
ErrGlobalAppApprovalRevoked, revoking is
ErrGlobalAppApprovalRevokingCascadeInProgress.

Tests
- verify TestRequireActiveGlobalAppApproval: each state goes through the
  account bytes and RequireCanonicalGlobalAppApproval. The Active control
  passes. Revoked (as the program writes it, and with no revoked_at),
  RevokingCascadeInProgress, and Active with a revoked_at (nonzero and zero)
  are each refused by their own sentinel and by no other one. An unknown
  status is refused.
- trustmaster TestR15c_AppApprovalMustBeActive: each non-Active state is
  ErrAppApprovalNotActive carrying its cause, and never ErrAppApprovalMismatch.
- trustmaster TestR15c_StatusIsDecidedBeforeTheClearances: with the author
  Blocked, a non-Active approval is refused as R-15c after one approval read
  and zero clearance reads. The control is the same world with the approval
  Active, where the Blocked author gives ErrBlacklisted.
- trustmaster TestE2E_RealChainReader_AppApprovalMustBeActive runs the real
  SolanaChain over RPC with Revoked, RevokingCascadeInProgress and Active with a
  revoked_at as account bytes.
- Full suites pass: identity-gate, attest (pda with MELUSINA_CONTRACTS_CHECKOUT
  on contracts origin/main), dns-sidecar and remotebak-sidecar.

Mutations: 16 were run and restored byte for byte (the tree diff hash was
unchanged). Each one fails by name:
- GrainCert skips R-15c; judges the status after the clearances; reports a
  non-Active approval as ErrAppApprovalMismatch.
- verify accepts RevokingCascadeInProgress; accepts Revoked; does not check
  revoked_at; checks revoked_at only when it is nonzero; accepts an unknown
  status; names Revoked as the cascade in progress; stops matching
  ErrStatusNotActive.
- Positive controls: the trustmaster fixture approval set to Revoked, the e2e
  approval bytes set to RevokingCascadeInProgress, and the verify Active
  approval set to Revoked.
- Vector: the revoking account's status changed (SHA drift); the revoking
  account dropped with the SHA re-pinned (the coverage guard catches it); the
  instructions blob recorded wrong (contracts provenance catches it).

Follow-up in other repos: consumers that vendor identity-gate verify (the Store
sidecar, AilaGoon) get RequireActiveGlobalAppApproval when they re-vendor. It
is new API, so nothing they vendor today changes behaviour. trustmaster has no
consumer outside this module.

